SCENE STRUCTURE (15 seconds total)

SCENE 0 - ANCHOR IMAGE (0.0–0.3s)
• thread-water ripples flow softly
• lanterns sway on their strings
• the boat rocks gently
• tree crowns pulse with faint bioluminescence
Camera: slow orbit, 15° arc, slight vertical drift.

SCENE 1 — The Drift Start (0.3–2.5s)

Low front-mounted camera on the girl’s boat.
Her oar dips into the luminous thread-water, causing long glowing ripples that weave around the hull.
Lantern reflections stretch into shimmering lines.

Motion: slow forward glide + gentle camera tilt.

SCENE 2 — The Awakening Current (2.5–5s)

Side-tracking shot following beside her boat.
The water suddenly brightens, forming luminous eddies that swirl like soft threads being pulled forward.
Villagers look up as the entire floating-market glows more intensely.

Camera: left-to-right tracking with foreground boats passing close for parallax.

SCENE 3 — Lantern Lift (5–8s)

Crane shot rising above her boat.
Hundreds of lanterns detach and float upward in spirals.
Their trails create volumetric vortex patterns in the dark sky.
Light reflections dance on the water, bending with the ripples.

Camera: slow upward lift + 30° rotation.

SCENE 4 — The Pull (8–11s)

Behind-the-boat chase shot.
The magical current speeds up; the water behaves like soft fabric being pulled taut.
Trees ripple with synchronized bioluminescent waves.

Camera: accelerating dolly forward, moving just above the water.

SCENE 5 — The Reveal (11–14s)

Through a gap in the glowing village, a gold-thread gateway appears upstream.
The structure radiates like woven sunlight.
Camera: controlled push-in, slight shake from the strong current.

Thread particles drift around the frame.

SCENE 6 — Rush into the Light (14–15s)

Fast whip-pan forward as the boat plunges into the golden gateway.
Frame blooms with warm white-gold light.
Lantern silhouettes streak past.

Cut end on a bright, expanding glow.

GOAL
A fast, cinematic journey through a glowing-thread floating market, filled with action, lantern magic, and dynamic camera moves — zero static shots.